tests/eval/gsm8k-200.jsonl

Derived from the first 200 items of the GSM8K test split
(grade_school_math/data/test.jsonl) in https://github.com/openai/grade-school-math,
commit 3101c7d5072418e28b9008a6636bde82a006892c. Each question is wrapped in a single
user message with an answer-format instruction; the answer is the number after "#### "
with thousands separators removed. Regenerate with scripts/eval/make-gsm8k-200.sh.

tests/eval/gsm8k-full.jsonl

The full GSM8K test split (1,319 items), downloaded from the Hugging Face dataset
https://huggingface.co/datasets/openai/gsm8k (config `main`, split `test`), revision
740312add88f781978c0658806c59bc2815b9866. Same wrapper, id scheme (`gsm8k-test-NNNN`)
and answer extraction as gsm8k-200.jsonl above — its first 200 items are byte-identical
to the committed gsm8k-200.jsonl. Regenerate with scripts/eval/make-gsm8k-full.sh
(downloads the dataset's test-split parquet file on demand; needs `hf` and `uv`, run on
novanas — the Hugging Face token lives there and nothing is uploaded).

tests/eval/gsm8k-200-completion.jsonl

The completion-form (no chat template) counterpart of gsm8k-200.jsonl, for base
checkpoints that have no chat template. Same 200 questions and answers, same source
and commit as gsm8k-200.jsonl above, fetched again to keep each item's full worked
solution (gsm8k-200.jsonl's jq filter keeps only the final number). Wraps each
question in a fixed 8-shot chain-of-thought completion prompt whose exemplars are
items 200..207 of the same source file (outside the 200 scored items), each rendered
as "Question: ... / <instruction> / <steps> / Answer: <number>" with the source's
calculator annotations (`<<...>>`) stripped; the scored item's prompt ends after the
instruction line, and the request carries `stop: ["\n\nQuestion:"]` so the model does
not run on into a new question. Regenerate with
scripts/eval/make-gsm8k-200-completion.sh.

